          "y": 68,
          "name": "Essay Top Image",
          "clip": true,
          "width": 300,
          "height": 156,
          "fill": {
            "type": "image",
            "enabled": true,
            "url": "images/generated-1786195484498.png",
            "mode": "fill"
          },
          "layout": "none"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "vc0U6",
          "x": 46,
          "y": 236,
          "name": "Essay Top Caption",
          "fill": "#70583F",
          "content": "LUNCH, BEFORE THE FIRST GUEST ARRIVES",
          "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Mono",
          "fontSize": 8,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.7
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "jGzIK",
          "x": 46,
          "y": 276,
          "name": "Essay Title",
          "fill": "#3A2A1D",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 470,
          "content": "Why we still set the table.",
          "lineHeight": 1,
          "fontFamily": "Playfair Display",
          "fontSize": 44,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "R6xhR",
          "x": 46,
          "y": 380,
          "name": "Essay Standfirst",
          "fill": "#8A5A30",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 410,
          "content": "A meal is more than a collection of plates. It is an invitation to slow the evening down.",
          "lineHeight": 1.2,
          "fontFamily": "Playfair Display",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "fontStyle": "italic"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "g1q0QG",
          "x": 46,
          "y": 452,
          "name": "Essay Byline",
          "fill": "#70583F",
          "content": "WORDS BY CLARA VOSS · PHOTOGRAPHS BY THE MARKET LANE KITCHEN",
          "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Mono",
          "fontSize": 8,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.6
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "mb0Fj",
          "x": 46,
          "y": 496,
          "name": "Essay Body",
          "fill": "#4E4038",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 355,
          "content": "There is a point in every service when the room changes. The door is still open, the wine is still being poured, but suddenly the table begins to make sense. Someone passes the bread. A knife finds the soft centre of a ripe cheese. The conversation gathers itself around the small, practical pleasure of sharing.\n\nAt the shop, we think often about the objects that make this possible. A board with room for one more wedge. A jar of something bright enough to interrupt the richness. Crackers that break cleanly between your fingers. None of these things are remarkable alone, but together they give the evening a shape.\n\nOur shelves are built with this thought in mind: not to make a perfect plate, but to make it easier to welcome people in. The best tables never look too arranged. They are generous, a little untidy, and always ready for another chair.",
          "lineHeight": 1.48,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "WeIY4",
          "x": 438,
          "y": 500,
          "name": "Essay Side Photo One",
          "clip": true,
          "width": 216,
          "height": 162,
          "fill": {
            "type": "image",
            "enabled": true,
            "url": "images/generated-1786195484565.png",
            "mode": "fill"
          },
          "layout": "none"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "dwIKs",
          "x": 438,
