          "fill": "#5D5A52",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 525,
          "content": "From Roman thermae to the Japanese ofuro, the history of bathing has always been a story about how a culture understands time, body and care.",
          "lineHeight": 1.48,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "N6NA6m",
          "x": 46,
          "y": 338,
          "name": "Historic Bath Image",
          "clip": true,
          "width": 608,
          "height": 190,
          "fill": {
            "type": "image",
            "enabled": true,
            "url": "images/generated-1786297329321.png",
            "mode": "fill"
          },
          "layout": "none"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "i274B",
          "x": 46,
          "y": 568,
          "name": "History Article Columns",
          "width": 608,
          "height": 214,
          "gap": 26,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "u3ijC",
              "name": "History Left Column",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 10,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "g9av4",
                  "name": "History First Paragraph",
                  "fill": "#34342F",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The earliest bathing rooms were collective spaces. In Rome, heat was a sequence: tepidarium, caldarium, frigidarium. Architecture guided the body through temperature, conversation and pause.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "w1p4rU",
                  "name": "History Pull Quote",
                  "fill": "#6B523A",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "“To bathe was to participate in public life.”",
                  "lineHeight": 1.1,
                  "fontFamily": "DM Serif Display",
                  "fontSize": 21,
                  "fontWeight": "normal",
                  "fontStyle": "italic"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "KtydK",
              "name": "History Right Column",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 10,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "HPzHB",
                  "name": "History Second Paragraph",
                  "fill": "#34342F",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Centuries later, the domestic bathroom became a laboratory for privacy. Porcelain, plumbing and the small luxury of hot water moved the ritual behind a closed door — but never made it less important.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "tTccT",
                  "name": "History Byline",
                  "fill": "#776B5D",
                  "content": "WORDS · STUDIO AQUA",
                  "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Mono",
                  "fontSize": 9,
                  "fontWeight": "normal",
                  "letterSpacing": 0.7
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "J2eUMF",
          "x": 46,
          "y": 850,
          "name": "History Footer",
          "fill": "#776B5D",
          "content": "AQUA / EDIT · HISTORY · 06",
          "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Mono",
          "fontSize": 9,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.8
        }
      ]
    },
